{
	"_readme": [
		"Shared INPUT corpus for the PHP↔JS grammar-twin check (tools/test/slot-fold-twin-test.php).",
		"Inputs only — no expected outputs. Expectations live in tools/test/slot-fold-test.php, which",
		"pins the PHP owner's behaviour; this corpus asks a narrower question: do both implementations",
		"produce the SAME thing. A case added here needs no expected value, which is the point — the",
		"cheapest possible way to widen twin coverage.",
		"Cover the FORM SPACE, not just the canonical example (the practice rule that caught the",
		"separator findings): bare read vs analog vs same; zero/one/multi-hop chains; with and without",
		"limit; free-form values carrying : | and inner brackets; hand-edited orderings; malformed input",
		"(the two sides must AGREE on rejection, not merely both work on good input)."
	],
