	"_emitStructsReadme": [
		"EMIT-from-STRUCT cases. The slot/chain sections above enter through PARSE, which normalizes",
		"every value to a string — so they cannot reach a control-side struct holding a NUMBER. That",
		"gap hid a real hazard: a JS `if (step.limit)` guard drops a numeric 0 (unlimited) while leaving",
		"the string '0' alone, so a parse-only corpus reports agreement. Guard on null/undefined, never",
		"truthiness — these rows are what proves it."
	],
